{
  "analysis": "objdump cannot disassemble MIPS because the installed objdump lacks MIPS support. The ELF layout is known: text/rodata at 0x400000, data/bss at 0x466520 with a very large BSS. The platform code saves /tmp/frame.bmp every 10 frames as a 32-bit BMP. I still need to inspect the custom stdlib/syscall layer and find a working disassembler if available.",
  "plan": "Inspect my_stdlib.c and my_stdlib.h to see how syscalls are invoked. Check for llvm-objdump or MIPS cross tools. If possible, disassemble syscall sites and key functions. Also dump symbols around DG_DrawFrame/writeBMPFile to confirm addresses.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '1,260p' /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/my_stdlib.h\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '1,420p' /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/my_stdlib.c\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "which llvm-objdump mips-linux-gnu-objdump mipsel-linux-gnu-objdump clang llc llvm-mc || true\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "readelf -s /app/doomgeneric_mips | grep -Ei \"writeBMPFile|DG_DrawFrame|fopen|fwrite|fclose|printf|fprintf|memset|memcpy|malloc|free|open|read|write|close|exit|brk|_start|__start|main\" | head -120\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '1,340p' /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/doomgeneric_img.c\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
